<%# `details` and `youtubeBlocked` are optional, so both are probed with typeof - a bare reference
    throws "not defined" for the callers that omit them and takes the whole render with it.

    details was passed by the sync route and never rendered here, so the one line that said when the
    quota resets has never reached the screen. The marker attribute is how the page learns to
    disable its sync and edit controls: this arrives inside an already-open SSE stream, so the
    HX-Trigger header the other routes use cannot be set by the time we know. %>
<div id="sync-result-<%= playlistId %>"<% if (typeof youtubeBlocked !== 'undefined' && youtubeBlocked) { %> data-youtube-blocked="true"<% } %>>
  <strong><%= title %></strong><% if (message) { %><br><%= message %><% } %>
  <% if (typeof details !== 'undefined' && details) { %><br><span class="small"><%= details %></span><% } %>
</div>
